---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="How to Use This Archive" description="A guide to navigating the Vedāntic Study Archive.">
  <div class="container page-pad">
    <h1>How to Use This Archive</h1>

    <section class="video-tours" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2>Video Guides</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        📹 Video tour guides are being prepared and will appear here. The layout structure is ready below.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          Desktop Tour (1 min)
        </h3>
        <div style="position:relative; padding-bottom:56.25%;
          height:0; overflow:hidden; border-radius:8px; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px dashed var(--border-color);">
          <iframe
            src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/DESKTOP_VIDEO_ID"
            style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;
              width:100%;height:100%;border:0;"
            allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write;
              encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
            allowfullscreen
            loading="lazy"
          ></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          Mobile Tour (50 sec)
        </h3>
        <div style="max-width: 360px;">
          <div style="position:relative; padding-bottom:177.78%;
            height:0; overflow:hidden; border-radius:8px; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px dashed var(--border-color);">
            <iframe
              src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/MOBILE_VIDEO_ID"
              style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;
                width:100%;height:100%;border:0;"
              allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write;
                encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
              allowfullscreen
              loading="lazy"
            ></iframe>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <h2>Who This Archive Is For</h2>
    <p>Students attending Swami Shankarananda's classes on Bṛhadāraṇyaka Upaniṣad. Also accessible to serious students of Advaita Vedānta with some familiarity with Sanskrit.</p>

    <h2>Navigating the Archive</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The Bṛhadāraṇyaka page lists all classes in order. Click any class to open its notes.</li>
      <li>Each class page shows: Coverage, Audio Player, Embedded Video, Source Text, and the full Notes.</li>
      <li>Use the IAST / Devanagari toggle to switch between Roman transliteration and Devanagari script at any time. Your preference is remembered across visits.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The Source Text Panel</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A floating button opens the Source Text panel.</li>
      <li>This shows the exact mantra, bhāṣyam, and vārtika covered in that class, colour-coded for easy reading.</li>
      <li>You can read the source text alongside the notes without losing your place.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Colour Coding in Source Text</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Black bold — Mūlam (the Upaniṣad mantra itself)</li>
      <li>Black normal — Bhāṣyam (Śaṅkara's commentary)</li>
      <li>Orange bold — Pratīka (mantra words quoted in bhāṣyam)</li>
      <li>Violet — Vārttika (Sureśvara's verse commentary)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The Glossary</h2>
    <p>The Glossary page lists Sanskrit terms explained by Swamiji, organised by class. Use it when you encounter an unfamiliar term in the notes.</p>

    <h2>Audio and Video</h2>
    <p>Each class has an audio player for the full class recording where audio is available. The embedded YouTube video appears directly on the class page when a video URL is present.</p>

    <h2>Offline Reading</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>In any browser, use File → Save Page As to save a class for offline reading. The text and formatting will be preserved.</li>
      <li>On mobile, use your browser's Add to Reading List or Save for Offline feature.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections and Feedback</h2>
    <p>If you notice any error in the notes or Sanskrit citations, please use the Feedback page to report it. Accuracy in representing the bhāṣya and mūla texts is the highest priority of this archive.</p>

    <h2>Pronunciation Help</h2>
    <p>If you are unfamiliar with IAST diacritics, visit the Pronunciation Guide page for a complete key to Sanskrit letters with English pronunciation examples.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
